## VSOP87B (Bureau des Longitudes, CDS VI/81) - the Jupiter and Saturn rows, and
## only those: the five rows JPL's approximate elements do hold are still ELEMENTS
## in planets.gd (see the tables there and data/SOURCES.md). Heliocentric ecliptic
## and equinox J2000, in astronomical units - the same frame ELEMENTS is written in,
## so a row swapped for these needs no conversion.
##
## One line per term, in the order the file gives them:
##     <body> <variable> <power> <A> <B> <C>     with the term  A*cos(B + C*T),
## T in Julian millennia from J2000 (365250 days). Truncated at A >= 1e-6 rad:
## 847 of the 5,300 terms survive, and the largest position error that drops out is
## 0.43 arcsec on 木星 and 0.24 arcsec on 土星 over 1800-2050 (measured against the
## untruncated series; planets.gd's A6 numbers are measured against Horizons).
